 buildings alone is projected to  surge to 14 billion dollars annually we  have aging municipal infrastructure that  breaks down when big storms hit we have  aging housing infrastructure and  increasingly so we're still  building in the wrong places as the  population increases we're building in  places that are vulnerable to flooding  in the wake of recent flooding  catastrophes there's a growing  recognition that national leadership and  a lot more money are needed to help  prepare for the extreme weather ahead  but in some flood-prone areas  preventative measures won't cut it  moving homes or entire communities away  from floodplains is the only solution  in merit mayor linda brown says that's  something they're now considering  we have people that are living in areas  now that are  a bigger flood plain than we could ever  imagine so we really have to talk about  moving some of them to drier land  we know the solutions the problem is  we're not mobilizing the solutions  nearly quickly enough therein lies the  problem for canada and if we don't do  that we are going to suffer  increasingly so due to extreme weather  events period there is no way to cheat  this system
 

